th a shaman, and German-Iranian cinematographer Faraz Fesharaki's directorial feature debut What Did You Dream Last Night, Parajanov, capturing his own family's diaspora experiences.\n\nThe line-up also features provocative Canadian filmmaker Bruce LaBruce's London-shot The Visitor, inspired by Pier Paolo Pasolini's Teorama, in which a stranger lands with a bourgeois family, and has"
