    "snippet": "---\ntitle: HIFF44 PRESENTS: FULL PROGRAMMING LINEUP\ndate: 2024-09-06\n---\nHIFF44 ANNOUNCES FEATURE FILM SELECTIONS, HONOREES, AND SIGNATURE PROGRAMMING\n\nThe Hawai'i International Film Festival presented by Halekulani celebrates its 44th year (HIFF44) as the premiere cinematic film festival in the Pacific with the theme \"Creating New Traditions\" highlighting the best in new cinema from Hawai'i, Asia, the Pacific Islands, and the world while blending the rich cultural heritage of the islands with innovative storytelling techniques and diverse perspectives. This year's festival will present 92 feature films, 114 shorts, 40 world premieres, and 31 U.S. premieres.\n\nHIFF44 presented by Halekulani runs October 2-13 in Honolulu and October 15-17 in West O\u02bbahu, followed by screenings October 19-20 on Maui, October 21-23 on Lana\u02bbi, November 1-3 on Kaua\u02bbi, November 2-3 on the Big Island (Waimea), November 7-8 on Moloka\u02bbi, and November 7-10 on the Big Island of Hawai\u02bbi (Hilo).\n\nHIFF44 GALA PRESENTATIONS:\n\nTIN\u0100 (MOTHER) \u2014 OPENING NIGHT FILM\n\nHIFF44 opens at the Consolidated Theatres Kahala with the World Premiere and directorial feature debut of Miki Magasiva's nuanced drama TIN\u0100 (MOTHER) from New Zealand/Aotearoa. Samoan actor Anapela Polata'ivao (ONE THOUSAND ROPES, OUR FLAG MEANS DEATH, SHORTLAND STREET) portrays Mareta, a well-respected and gifted vocal coach in her community, who finds herself at a crossroads, needing to find work after the tragic death of her daughter, a death she is still processing. Mareta goes out of her comfort zone to become a substitute teacher at an elite, all-white private school and forms a choir that begins her healing as a matriarch and caregiver. Director Miki Magasiva and actress Anapela Polata'ivao are scheduled to attend HIFF44 Opening Night.\n\nNew Zealand/Aotearoa 2024 | English, Samoan w/English Subtitles | 124M\n\nMOLOKA'I BOUND \u2014 CENTERPIECE PRE"
